    "standardized_narrative": "The syndicate experienced an overall deterioration of GBP 4.1 million in its prior year reserves, representing a 1.25% strengthening against opening gross claims outstanding. This adverse development was primarily driven by deteriorations in third party liability (GBP 2.0 million), marine, aviation and transport (GBP 2.8 million), and fire and other damage to property (GBP 3.4 million). These were partially offset by favourable developments (releases) in energy (GBP 2.2 million) and reinsurance acceptances (GBP 1.8 million). Specific prior year events contributing to the adverse development on the 2016 year of account included Hurricanes Harvey, Irma, Maria, and Cyclone Debbie (all 2017 events), a contract frustration loss for Trafigura, a power transformer fire in Columbia, and various large single casualty claims. Favourable development was noted for 2015 and prior years, and further releases were made from reserves related to the 2001 World Trade Centre litigation. However, a yacht fire in Germany in late 2018 also impacted back years.",
    "raw_causal_phrases": [
